<title>UK: Denmark sets 10 billion yen two-year bond.</title>
<headline>Denmark sets 10 billion yen two-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Sanwa International and Kukusai (Europe).</p>
<p> BORROWER   DENMARK</p>
<p> AMT    10.0 BLN YEN  COUPON     7.0	 MATURITY    29.SEP.98</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE  L-26.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    =	   L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (M) ONE     SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/NZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    =	   SELL CONC  1.50	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p> NOTES	REDEMPTION IN NEW ZEALAND DOLLARS</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
